## 🔹 Chapter 4: Keyboard Shortcuts

| Shortcut | Action |
|----------|--------|
| `Ctrl + C` | Stops a running command |
| `Ctrl + L` | Clears the terminal screen (same as `clear`) |
| `↑` (Up Arrow) | Recalls previous commands |

> 🎬 **Live Scenario:** You accidentally started an endless process like `ping google.com`. Instead of closing the terminal, press `Ctrl + C`.
>
> Instead of retyping `sudo systemctl restart nginx`, press `↑` and hit **Enter**.

