## 🔹 Chapter 11: Redirecting Output (`>`)

Instead of printing to the screen, redirect output into a file.

```bash
whoami > user.txt
hostname > host.txt
cat host.txt
```

**Output:**
```
prod-web01
```

> 🎬 **Live Scenario — Server Audit**
>
> ```bash
> mkdir -p /root/answers
> cd /root/answers
>
> whoami > user.txt
> hostname > host.txt
> uname -s > kernel.txt
> ls / > root-listing.txt
> cat /etc/os-release > os.txt
> ```
>
> This creates five files you can share with the operations team or attach to a support ticket — no manual copy-pasting needed.

